<Application x:Class="Bws.Gui.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:ui="http://schemas.lepo.co/wpfui/2022/xaml"
             StartupUri="MainWindow.xaml">

    <!--
        ADR-24. The base of this window's appearance is WPF UI, not the Fluent theme built into
        WPF, and docs/10-WPF-UI.md is required reading before this file changes.

        THERE IS NO ThemeMode HERE AND THERE MUST NOT BE. It is not a leftover. ThemeMode="Dark"
        together with the dictionaries below KILLS THE PROCESS at startup, with
        InvalidOperationException out of ThemeManager.ApplyStyleOnWindow saying
        AllowsTransparency cannot be changed after the window is shown.

        Removing it also fixed something nobody had connected to it: ThemeMode applies a MICA
        backdrop, a window with Mica is translucent to the desktop compositor, and WPF turns
        ClearType OFF on a translucent surface. Measured by counting text pixels carrying
        colour fringing - 0% before, 80.5% after. That was the blurry text.

        Theme.xaml is merged LAST on purpose: a dictionary merged later wins, and ours holds
        the values that are ours. It also no longer loads on its own, because it resolves keys
        that arrive with ControlsDictionary.
    -->
    <Application.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <ui:ThemesDictionary Theme="Dark" />
                <ui:ControlsDictionary />
                <ResourceDictionary Source="Themes/Theme.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Application.Resources>
</Application>
